  "snippet": "#​498 — November 20, 2026 Read on the Web React Status React Flow 13: Fewer Re-Renders for Big Node-Based UIs — The library behind countless node editors and workflow UIs gets its first major release in two years, with n...",
  "coverImage": "https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/ds7cbagrj5mmhgomkj4i.jpg",
  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​498 — November 20, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193238/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the Web</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<div style=\"color: #333;\">\n<div style=\"font-size: 2.7em; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.3em; margin-bottom: 0px;\"> React Status</div>\n</div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193203/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/ds7cbagrj5mmhgomkj4i.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193203/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.4em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"xyflow.com\">React Flow 13: Fewer Re-Renders for Big Node-Based UIs</a></span> — The library behind countless node editors and workflow UIs gets its first major release in two years, with new hooks like <code>useNode</code> that cut unnecessary re-renders in large flows.</p>\n<p>Hayleigh Thompson (xyflow) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>💡 If you're an existing user, there's <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193204/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">a migration guide</a>. <em>Vue Flow</em> has also now joined the xyflow family, alongside <em>Svelte Flow</em>.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193202/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"80\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/f168661f.webp\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"160\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193202/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"sentry.io\">How to Build Your Own Automated Debugging Workflow</a></span> — Factory, Exa, and Bolt connected their coding agents to Sentry so production errors become fix PRs, not tickets. Get the recipes for Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, or bring your own coding agent.</p>\n<p>Sentry <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193205/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"nextjs.org\">Why Next.js Has Had 51 Security Advisories This Year</a></span> — You've surely noticed Next.js is getting a <em>lot</em> of security releases recently, but why? Unsurprisingly, it's AI, which is making old bugs easier to find, with 70% of this year's vulnerabilities found in code at least a year old. The team explains how it's responding and helping us stay up to date.</p>\n<p>The Next.js Team </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>⚠️ In related news, a campaign dubbed <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193206/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">React2STEAL</a> is exploiting servers that are still unpatched against React2Shell and the old middleware bypass, in order to publish their secrets. <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193207/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Here's what to check</a> on your apps.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><span>🎬</span> <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193208/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.remotion.dev\">Remotion Studio is Now a Visual Editor That Writes Back to Code</a></span> — Remotion lets you make videos programmatically with React code, and this short video shows off how its <em>Studio</em> now works like a timeline editor, where you can drag/trim/keyframe something with the edit written back to your source. <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193209/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">Your own components can also join in</a>.</p>\n<p>Jonny Burger </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193210/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">When an Import Becomes a Zip Bomb: Catching Bundle Regressions in Next.js</a> – By setting up per-route JavaScript budgets in CI. <cite>Sergey Patrakeev</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193211/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">React 19.3's View Transitions, Tested: What Actually Animates?</a> – Hint: not a plain <code>setState</code>. <cite>Esteban Trillo</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193212/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Shared Element Transitions Grow Up in Reanimated 4.8</a> – Now on by default, and they move the real view. <cite>Bartłomiej Błoniarz (Software Mansion)</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>🛠  Code, Tools &amp; Libraries</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193213/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/eekvnbhdbukialvphr1t.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193213/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"react-anatomy.com\">React Anatomy: Explode a React Page into 3D Layers</a></span> — A DevTools extension that splits a running React page into 3D layers mapped to the components that rendered it, with live props for whatever you click. You can <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193214/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">try the demo</a> without installing anything.</p>\n<p>Nicolas Charpentier </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193215/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"stepperize.com\">Stepperize 9.0: Type-Safe Multi-Step Flows for React</a></span> — A popular library for wizards, checkouts and onboarding where you define steps once and get typed navigation, plus guards that block a user from advancing until a step is valid.</p>\n<p>Damian Ricobelli </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193216/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"fate.technology\">Fate 2.0: The Async React Data Client Now Handles Client State Too</a></span> — The Relay-inspired data client now manages client-only and offline state through the same views and mutations as server data, and works as a GraphQL client too. It's already replaced Relay and TinyBase in Christoph's game, <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193217/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">Athena Crisis</a>.</p>\n<p>Christoph Nakazawa </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193218/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"detent.hayder.sh\">Detent: A Wheel Picker for React with Real Inertia</a></span> — An iOS-style wheel picker that uses its own physics rather than <code>scroll-snap</code>, meaning that a 'throw' has momentum and lands cleanly on options. The demo on the homepage is very cute and worth… a spin. 😎</p>\n<p>Hayder </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193219/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/syuisr0pjgfgzjub1sks.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>📊 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193219/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Recharts 3.11</a> <em>(above)</em> – Popular charting library. Now with <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193220/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">context-based themes</a> and accessible fill patterns.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>⚠️ <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193221/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">React Router 8.5.2</a> and <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193222/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">7.18.6</a> – Upgrade to either version for fixes covering <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193223/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">seven security advisories</a>, four rated high.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193224/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">You Might Not Need an Effect 1.2</a> – ESLint plugin that flags unnecessary <code>useEffect</code> calls. Now 'sees through' popular third-party effect wrappers.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193225/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">ka-table 13.0</a> – Lightweight React table component. Now a keyboard-accessible ARIA grid and has added fixed columns and virtual scrolling of columns.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193226/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Redux Toolkit 2.15</a> – Each store now gets its own RTK Query runtime, fixing long-standing SSR and test isolation problems.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>📱 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193227/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">React Native Bottom Sheet 1.0</a> – Software Mansion's bottom sheet goes stable.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>🔥 Let the cloud take the heat. <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193228/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Expo Simulators</a> runs iOS simulators and Android emulators for your agents, and your laptop’s RAM stays free.</p>\n<p>⚡ Next.js, Astro or React Router site? <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193229/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Fimo</a> hosts it and runs AI agents that keep it found on Google and in AI answers.</p>\n<p>🎬 Your app needs video, not a video team. Upload any format to <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193230/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Hyperserve's API</a>, get back MP4 on a global CDN. Ship video in an afternoon.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>📢  Elsewhere in the ecosystem</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>The Next.js team is <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193231/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">experimenting with Switchyard</a>, a Go-powered server that <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193239/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">sits in front of <code>next start</code></a>. Currently, it forwards requests to Node, but the plan is to move routing work out of Node and into Switchyard. If you're self-hosting Next.js, this is one for your long-term radar.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193232/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Solid 2.0 is now stable</a>. Async is now part of the signals graph and server functions have moved into core. There are also new diagnostics aimed at coding agents.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>If you want to try speeding up your npm package installs, vlt's registry mirror <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193233/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">serves much less metadata</a>, making clean installs 20-70% faster and, now, <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193234/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">it's open for all to use</a> with no account/token needed.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🐘 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193235/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">PostgreSQL 19 is finally here!</a> If Postgres is part of your stack, our sister newsletter <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193236/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Postgres Weekly</em> covered it in depth this week</a> (please subscribe! 😅)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/193237/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">npkill 1.0</a> (<code>npx npkill</code>) no longer just clears out old <code>node_modules</code> folders, but build output and caches like <code>.next</code> and <code>.turbo</code> too.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
  "attachments": []
}